<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="viewer-lineup-tactics" data-rev="0">
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> web/lineup.mjs + tests</summary><div class="pl-card">Pure lineup legality: eleven starters, a goalkeeper, no player twice, bench at most seven; one reason at a time for the inline message. Ready now.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web logic</td><td>+260</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> web/pending.mjs + tests</summary><div class="pl-card">The pending-change list mirrors the engine queue by queue id: Queued, Applies now, Applied, Rejected, each chip carrying its word. Ready now.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web logic</td><td>+220</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/components/chip.css</summary><div class="pl-card">Chip styles from the token file; colour never carries the state alone.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web page</td><td>+60</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> lineup editor, tactics panel, substitution picker</summary><div class="pl-card">Ordinary DOM, keyboard operable, click-to-place first. Blocked on the two open contract questions.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web panels</td><td>+630</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/index.html, web/main.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Editor and panel regions, the test-hook readers, and product wording in place of an internal placeholder note.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>web page</td><td>+100 / -10</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> protocol, session, serve, protocol reference</summary><div class="pl-card">Pending the product owner: how a squad reaches the page, how a lineup returns before kick-off, and where the tactics schema lives.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>engine side</td><td>open</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>No path carries a chosen lineup to the engine.</strong> The match is built from the team files before any page connects and starts producing at once; the answer to the first open question sets the contract.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Tactics schema is shared with a sibling plan in flight.</strong> The change payload and the substitution count must match what the tactics work emits.</aside>
  </div>

  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>0 prior revisions</summary><ul></ul></details>

  <style>
    .fragment-plan .pl-files { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files th, .fragment-plan .pl-files td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); vertical-align: top; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files summary { cursor: pointer; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-chip { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid currentColor; margin-right: 6px; opacity: 0.8; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-card { padding: 6px 0 4px 18px; opacity: 0.9; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-risks { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-revs { margin-top: 12px; }
    @media (max-width: 480px) { .fragment-plan .pl-files th:nth-child(3), .fragment-plan .pl-files td:nth-child(3) { display: none; } }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-plan');
      var files = 14, modules = 8;
      var risks = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.pl-risks .callout').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'plan', artifact: 'plan', counts: { files: files, modules: modules, risks: risks } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
